KG42.register("clusters-29a3eed41fee5d52b58f79b3",{"id":"20-storage_sharing_auction::v142-d-CL002","paper":"20-storage_sharing_auction","label":"Coordination of price and supply response and the unit payment obligation","record":{"cluster_id":"v142-d-CL002","label":"Coordination of price and supply response and the unit payment obligation","market_meaning":"Given the participating group and the price bounds, the auctioneer selects the price based on the SFC average cost saving, and RU selects the shared energy storage quantity accordingly; the resulting auction price also serves as the unit price paid by SFC to RU. The candidate includes price selection, supply response, and the unit payment obligation, but its bounded equilibrium calculation has not yet been closed.","mechanism_ids":["v141-a-M01"],"market_types":["LEM"],"process_stages":["coordination","matching","pricing","settlement"],"scope_disposition":"conditional","scope_explanation":"The main assembly applies to the same auction after excluding marginal participants. R004 provides only the participating-group interface, and R002 provides the responsible entity; the branch in R004 that allows marginal participation is not automatically applied to the existing pricing summation scope. Per-time-slot reuse is limited to the price and response within the same time slot and is not equivalent to a complete cross-time-slot model.","assembly_status":"partial","boundary_rationale":"Price signals, RU response, and the auctioneer objective have direct decision coupling, and the payment chain explicitly takes up the same unit price, so they are combined into one cluster. The overlapping response formulations in R003 and R005 are not counted as an additional independent rule; participant screening and actual quantity allocation retain separate boundaries.","chain_bindings":[{"chain_id":"v141-c-R003","ownership":"primary","role":"support","rationale":"Supplement price publication and bounded RU response; the response formulation repeated with R005 is retained as a comparable reference and is not counted as an additional independent market rule."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R005","ownership":"primary","role":"core","rationale":"Carry the auctioneer's price decision, cost-saving objective, and pricing expression coupled with RU response."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R006","ownership":"primary","role":"core","rationale":"Interpret the auction price as the unit payment obligation borne by SFC to RU and do not extend it to a total billing rule that is not provided."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R004","ownership":"shared","role":"interface","rationale":"Only reference the already determined participation cutoff, group, and bid inputs; the main attribution of the screening decision remains in v142-d-CL001."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R002","ownership":"shared","role":"support","rationale":"Reference the responsibility of the same third-party auctioneer to specify the price decision responsibility; do not add institutional conditions that it must satisfy."}],"connections":[{"connection_id":"v142-d-CL002-L01","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R002","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R005","kind":"functional_coupling","from_refs":["v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C001"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R005::phi::v141-c-R005-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E20","v141-b-g01-E22","v141-b-g01-E36"],"rationale":"The same auctioneer organizes the transaction according to established rules and bears the specific responsibility of selecting the auction price for SFC."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-CL002-L02","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R004","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R005","kind":"quantity_interface","from_refs":["v141-c-R004::x::v141-c-R004-x-J","v141-c-R004::x::v141-c-R004-x-K","v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C003"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R005::theta::v141-c-R005-th-J","v141-c-R005::theta::v141-c-R005-th-K","v141-c-R005::phi::v141-c-R005-C006"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E05","v141-b-g02-E07","v141-b-g02-E13","v141-b-g02-E14"],"rationale":"The cutoff obtained from screening defines the participation scope of the price game and enters the cost-saving objective. Here only the quantity and scope of the same auction are passed, and the cutoff is not mistaken for the actual number of participants after excluding marginal parties."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-CL002-L03","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R005","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R003","kind":"quantity_interface","from_refs":["v141-c-R005::x::v141-c-R005-x-p","v141-c-R005::phi::v141-c-R005-C005"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R003::x::v141-c-R003-x-p_t","v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E22","v141-b-g02-E13"],"rationale":"The price decision in the payment rule serves as the price signal published to RU in the same auction; the local roles of price selection and signal publication are still retained separately."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-CL002-L04","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R003","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R005","kind":"functional_coupling","from_refs":["v141-c-R003::x::v141-c-R003-x-x_i","v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C002"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R005::x::v141-c-R005-x-xi","v141-c-R005::phi::v141-c-R005-C006"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E14","v141-b-g02-E19"],"rationale":"The bounded quantity response made by RU as a function of price enters the auctioneer's cost-saving calculation, so this is decision coupling rather than merely narrative sequence. In the original chains, the price and signal edges in the opposite direction are both retained and are not deduplicated as the same edge."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-CL002-L05","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R003","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R005","kind":"alternative_representation","from_refs":["v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C002","v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C004"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R005::phi::v141-c-R005-C007"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E11","v141-b-g02-E17","v141-b-g02-E19"],"rationale":"The two chains express the same RU response, but the applicable conditions of the bounded optimization and the direct closed-form response are not aligned; R005 further writes the two as equal, so they are only associated as different formulations to be explained."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-CL002-L06","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R005","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R006","kind":"quantity_interface","from_refs":["v141-c-R005::x::v141-c-R005-x-p"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R006::x::v141-c-R006-x-p_t","v141-c-R006::phi::v141-c-R006-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E22","v141-b-g02-E14"],"rationale":"The citation explicitly interprets the price selected by the auctioneer as the unit price paid by SFC to RU; this interface does not produce a total payment amount or a billing formula for allocated quantity."}],"object_mappings":[{"mapping_id":"v142-d-CL002-M01","kind":"same_node","member_refs":["v141-c-R002::V::coordination.local_operator","v141-c-R004::V::coordination.local_operator","v141-c-R005::V::coordination.local_operator"],"canonical_ref":"v141-c-R004::V::coordination.local_operator","display_policy":"single_representative","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E20","v141-b-g02-E05","v141-b-g01-E36"],"rationale":"The entity organizing the auction, determining the group, and selecting the price is the auctioneer in the same mechanism; only the node display is unified."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-CL002-M02","kind":"same_node","member_refs":["v141-c-R004::V::matching.counterparties","v141-c-R005::V::matching.counterparties"],"canonical_ref":"v141-c-R004::V::matching.counterparties","display_policy":"single_representative","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E05","v141-b-g02-E05","v141-b-g02-E13"],"rationale":"The participant determination activity referenced by the pricing chain is exactly the screening activity of R004 and does not represent another round of automatic re-matching."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-CL002-M03","kind":"same_node","member_refs":["v141-c-R003::V::pricing.local","v141-c-R005::V::pricing.local","v141-c-R006::V::pricing.local"],"canonical_ref":"v141-c-R005::V::pricing.local","display_policy":"single_representative","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E22","v141-b-g02-E13","v141-b-g02-E14"],"rationale":"All three chains revolve around the pricing activity of the same energy storage sharing auction and respectively present coordination, decision-making, and unit payment use."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-CL002-M04","kind":"same_node","member_refs":["v141-c-R003::V::coordination.price_signal","v141-c-R005::V::coordination.price_signal"],"canonical_ref":"v141-c-R003::V::coordination.price_signal","display_policy":"single_representative","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E13","v141-b-g02-E19"],"rationale":"Both places denote the same activity in which the auction price coordinates RU quantity selection; their original edges with different directions are not merged."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-CL002-M05","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R003::x::v141-c-R003-x-p_t","v141-c-R005::x::v141-c-R005-x-p","v141-c-R006::x::v141-c-R006-x-p_t"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E22","v141-b-g02-E13","v141-b-g02-E14"],"rationale":"The source text points selection, publication, and payment use to the same unit price of the same auction. The local roles and index differences of each chain are retained, and prices in different time slots are not equated on this basis."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-CL002-M06","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R003::x::v141-c-R003-x-x_i","v141-c-R005::x::v141-c-R005-x-xi"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E13","v141-b-g02-E17","v141-b-g02-E19"],"rationale":"Under the same participating RU and the same candidate price, both refer to RU's shared quantity strategy; they are not equivalent to an arbitrary strategy, the equilibrium realization value, or the final cleared quantity."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-CL002-M07","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R004::theta::v141-c-R004-theta-r-i","v141-c-R003::theta::v141-c-R003-theta-r_i","v141-c-R005::theta::v141-c-R005-th-r"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E09","v141-b-g02-E04","v141-b-g02-E11"],"rationale":"In the same auction, the reserve price submitted by RU is used both for screening and for response utility; these local inputs remain independently referenced and are not generalized to reserve prices after cross-time-slot updates."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-CL002-M08","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R003::theta::v141-c-R003-theta-alpha_i","v141-c-R005::theta::v141-c-R005-th-alpha"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E11","v141-b-g02-E17"],"rationale":"Both places are the same reluctance-to-share coefficient in the same RU response utility; associating them as the same quantity does not supply the coefficient conditions missing from the original chain."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-CL002-M09","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R003::theta::v141-c-R003-theta-b_i","v141-c-R005::theta::v141-c-R005-th-b"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E08","v141-b-g02-E17","v141-b-g02-E19"],"rationale":"In the same auction, both are strategic upper bounds on the RU's shareable space; they are not merged with per-time-slot available quantity or final allocated quantity."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-CL002-M10","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R004::theta::v141-c-R004-theta-a-m","v141-c-R005::theta::v141-c-R005-th-a"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E10","v141-b-g02-E04","v141-b-g02-E14"],"rationale":"The bid submitted by the same SFC in this auction is first used for screening and then for cost-saving calculation; both uses are retained."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-CL002-M11","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R004::x::v141-c-R004-x-J","v141-c-R005::theta::v141-c-R005-th-J"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E05","v141-b-g02-E07","v141-b-g02-E13"],"rationale":"The RU cutoff output from the screening stage becomes a pricing input; the local roles of decision variable and parameter are not merged, and the cutoff is different from the actual number of participants after excluding marginal parties."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-CL002-M12","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R004::x::v141-c-R004-x-K","v141-c-R005::theta::v141-c-R005-th-K"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E05","v141-b-g02-E07","v141-b-g02-E14"],"rationale":"The SFC cutoff output from the screening stage becomes a pricing input; only the cutoff of the same auction is connected, while the variable and parameter roles are maintained."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-CL002-M13","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R003::theta::v141-c-R003-theta-p_t_min","v141-c-R005::theta::v141-c-R005-th-pmin","v141-c-R006::theta::v141-c-R006-theta-pmin"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E35","v141-b-g02-E13","v141-b-g02-E14"],"rationale":"All three places reference the Vickrey lower bound within the same participation scope; this association does not confirm that it has already been defined in small samples or other participation branches."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-CL002-M14","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R003::theta::v141-c-R003-theta-p_t_max","v141-c-R005::theta::v141-c-R005-th-pmax","v141-c-R006::theta::v141-c-R006-theta-pmax"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E35","v141-b-g02-E09","v141-b-g02-E13","v141-b-g02-E14"],"rationale":"All three places use the price upper bound of that auction; the determination of the bound before the start of the payment rule is not mistakenly written as an activity after price optimization."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-CL002-M15","kind":"same_expression","member_refs":["v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C003","v141-c-R005::phi::v141-c-R005-C005","v141-c-R006::phi::v141-c-R006-C002"],"canonical_ref":"v141-c-R005::phi::v141-c-R005-C005","display_policy":"single_representative","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E35","v141-b-g02-E13","v141-b-g02-E14","v141-b-g02-E19"],"rationale":"Under the same auction and the same price bound, all three places express the same price-domain restriction; only a display representative of the mathematical restriction is selected, while R006's payment obligation and all original constraints are retained."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-CL002-M16","kind":"alternative_representation","member_refs":["v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C002","v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C004","v141-c-R005::phi::v141-c-R005-C007"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E17","v141-b-g02-E19"],"rationale":"These constraints express the same RU best response, but they are respectively a bounded optimization, a closed-form response, and a composite equality formulation of the two; boundary applicability has not been resolved, so no representative can be selected and unconditional equivalence cannot be claimed."}],"gaps":[{"gap_id":"v142-d-CL002-G01","category":"math_incomplete","description":"R003's bounded optimization and its closed-form response are not automatically equivalent, yet R005-C007 directly writes the two as equal. The price bound does not guarantee that each RU's closed-form response is nonnegative and does not exceed capacity; the original chain also does not fully list the conditions for strict concavity and capacity feasibility.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R003","v141-c-R005"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C002","v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C004","v141-c-R005::phi::v141-c-R005-C007"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E11","v141-b-g02-E17","v141-b-g02-E19"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Upstream shall verify the coefficient and capacity conditions, distinguish interior and boundary responses, and explain the applicable scope of the closed-form expression; this time the original formula is retained, and no truncated response is added."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-CL002-G02","category":"math_incomplete","description":"R005-C008 is obtained by substituting the closed-form response into the objective, but it does not handle the case where a price-interval endpoint or the RU capacity constraint becomes active, so a globally unique bounded equilibrium cannot be confirmed on this basis. Equation (10) in E15 fixes the response when comparing prices, whereas E18 uses a response that varies with price; the two equilibrium interpretations have not been aligned. When there are too few participants, the denominator of the average and the second-highest price may also be undefined.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R003","v141-c-R004","v141-c-R005"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R005::phi::v141-c-R005-C005","v141-c-R005::phi::v141-c-R005-C006","v141-c-R005::phi::v141-c-R005-C008","v141-c-R005::theta::v141-c-R005-th-pmin","v141-c-R004::x::v141-c-R004-x-J","v141-c-R004::x::v141-c-R004-x-K"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E35","v141-b-g02-E13","v141-b-g02-E15","v141-b-g02-E17","v141-b-g02-E18","v141-b-g02-E19"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Upstream shall check the leader's treatment of the response, constrained optimality, and uniqueness conditions, and specify the non-degenerate participation scale and small-sample handling; the source theorem is retained as a claim pending verification."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-CL002-G03","category":"scope_conflict","description":"The narratives of E37 and E10 write both ends of the price interval as lower bounds, whereas E13, E14, and E19 use an interval with upper and lower bounds. Frozen C currently uses the latter, but the available materials are insufficient to determine whether the former is a typesetting issue or a transcription issue.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R003","v141-c-R005","v141-c-R006"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C003","v141-c-R005::phi::v141-c-R005-C005","v141-c-R006::phi::v141-c-R006-C002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E37","v141-b-g02-E10","v141-b-g02-E13","v141-b-g02-E14","v141-b-g02-E19"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Manual review shall check the original intervals and contexts at these locations; retain the current C expression and the record of differences, and do not silently correct the B citation."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-CL002-G04","category":"upstream_missing","description":"R006 specifies only the unit payment price and does not provide the total payment amount, cost sharing, or billed quantity basis for each SFC or each RU. The R005 objective uses the RU response quantity, but subsequent allocation may reduce the actually shared quantity; therefore this objective quantity cannot be directly treated as the settled quantity or realized revenue.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R005","v141-c-R006"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R005::x::v141-c-R005-x-xi","v141-c-R005::phi::v141-c-R005-C006","v141-c-R006::phi::v141-c-R006-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E22","v141-b-g02-E14","v141-b-g02-E20"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"If a complete settlement or an explanation of realized benefits is required, upstream shall confirm the actual billed quantity, the amounts for both buyer and seller, and the utility basis after allocation; this cluster retains only the unit payment obligation."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-CL002-G05","category":"ontology_extension","description":"The price signal and auctioneer node are insufficient to express the leader-follower equilibrium structure on their own. proposal:v141-b-g01-P03 has still not been approved and cannot become a new scientific node through this assembly.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R003","v141-c-R005"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R003::V::coordination.price_signal","v141-c-R005::phi::v141-c-R005-C007","v141-c-R005::phi::v141-c-R005-C008"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E36","v141-b-g02-E13"],"proposal_ids":["proposal:v141-b-g01-P03"],"required_work":"Manual review shall check whether the mechanism expression needs to be extended; before approval, the leader and follower meaning is retained only through existing chain references and assembly descriptions."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-CL002-G06","category":"unverified_source","description":"The price, utility, equilibrium, and payment citations in this cluster all retain unverified status. Candidate mappings do not mean that the B transcription, C2 content, or unique-equilibrium claim has been independently reviewed.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R002","v141-c-R003","v141-c-R004","v141-c-R005","v141-c-R006"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C002","v141-c-R005::phi::v141-c-R005-C006","v141-c-R005::phi::v141-c-R005-C008","v141-c-R006::phi::v141-c-R006-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E22","v141-b-g02-E13","v141-b-g02-E14","v141-b-g02-E15","v141-b-g02-E17","v141-b-g02-E18","v141-b-g02-E19"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Subsequent manual review shall check, item by item, the sources, mathematical applicability conditions, and same-quantity mappings; experimental candidate status must not replace scientific confirmation."}]},"rule_refs":["20-storage_sharing_auction::v141-c-R003","20-storage_sharing_auction::v141-c-R005","20-storage_sharing_auction::v141-c-R006","20-storage_sharing_auction::v141-c-R004","20-storage_sharing_auction::v141-c-R002"],"unresolved_rule_refs":[],"node_ids":["COMP-6057789601b08e93","COMP-72f84a438787fbd5","COMP-bebd346528bbcf18","KG31-e2bea6d6e2936fab","KG40-404d7eddbf0fc37c"]});
